--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NOTE: the build brief assumed V1 = 3.31.5. Reading the real source shows the
CVE-2026-31816 fix in server/middleware/utils.ts is BYTE-IDENTICAL between
3.31.4 and 3.31.5 and first lands at 3.32.0. Corrected, source-accurate model:

  V0 = budibase/budibase:3.31.5  server/utils.ts UNANCHORED + backend-core/matchers.ts UNANCHORED
  V1 = budibase/budibase:3.32.0  CVE-2026-31816 fix anchors utils.ts; matchers.ts byte-identical to V0 (TARGET)
  V2 = budibase/budibase:3.35.4  CVE-2026-48147 fix anchors matchers.ts

Source diffs (raw.githubusercontent.com/Budibase/budibase/<tag>):
  server/middleware/utils.ts        : 3.31.4==3.31.5 (unanchored) ; 3.32.0==3.35.4 (anchored)  -> CVE-2026-31816 fixed @ 3.32.0
  backend-core/middleware/matchers.ts: 3.31.5==3.32.0 (unanchored) ; changed @ 3.35.4           -> CVE-2026-48147 fixed @ 3.35.4

  matchers.ts (V0/V1, vulnerable):
    return { regex: new RegExp(route), method, route }   // UNANCHORED
    const urlMatch = regex.test(ctx.request.url)         // FULL URL incl. query string
  matchers.ts (V2, fixed):
    return { regex: new RegExp(`^${route}`), method, route }
    const urlMatch = regex.test(ctx.path)

  csrf.ts (all versions): const found = matches(ctx, noCsrfOptions); if (found) return next()  // SKIP CSRF
  worker api/routes/index.ts: NO_CSRF_ENDPOINTS includes { route:"/api/global/auth/:tenantId" }
    -> buildMatcherRegex compiles to the unanchored  /api/global/auth/.*

